# Committed bundles are verified by sha256 against what CI built. Without this, a Windows
# checkout converts LF->CRLF and every hash taken there disagrees with the repository —
# which cost one QA run a false "the agent did not run our bytes" scare. Execution is
# unaffected (Node runs CRLF fine); what this protects is VERIFIABILITY, the whole reason
# dist/ is committed and checked for reproducibility.
* text=auto eol=lf
plugins/*/dist/** -text
